# mcp-ssh-manager server definitions.
# Bind-mounted read-only to /home/node/.ssh-manager/.env inside the devcontainer
# (the first entry in mcp-ssh-manager's env fallback chain).
# Format: SSH_SERVER_<NAME>_<FIELD> — see https://www.npmjs.com/package/mcp-ssh-manager
# Edits take effect after restarting the Claude Code session (the MCP child loads this once at startup).
# No secret lives here: KEYPATH points at a key bind-mounted from the host per devcontainer.json.

# Server: pulse — the runtime VM every agent stack is deployed to, one directory per agent
# under /app. Access is root by the owner's choice, so mcp__ssh-manager is deliberately NOT
# auto-approved in .claude/settings.json: every remote command needs human confirmation.
# See kb/architecture/ssh-mcp.md.
SSH_SERVER_PULSE_HOST=app.pulse-ai.live
SSH_SERVER_PULSE_USER=root
SSH_SERVER_PULSE_PORT=22
SSH_SERVER_PULSE_KEYPATH=/home/node/.ssh/pulse-vm-agent
SSH_SERVER_PULSE_DEFAULT_DIR=/app
SSH_SERVER_PULSE_DESCRIPTION="Pulse AI runtime VM (agent stacks under /app)"
